    #
    # words) failed the guard's END-TO-END test on both seeds (pooled cos 0.577, txtfusion.layerwise grad ratio 0.44-0.48, the
    # two passes' model outputs not bit-identical: rel 2.8e-3) while the strict LOCAL test passed (min cos 0.999994): the run
    # fell back to the old path + checkpointing (2.52 s/step vs ~1.2). 'full' (default): the trainer unchanged. 'local': the
    # verdict from the LOCAL test only (the end-to-end numbers are still computed and logged). 'aa': a third pass on the old
    # path (A/A) plus per-prompt output identity and the first LoRA Linears whose forward outputs differ (fast vs old, old vs
    # old) in one private line; the verdict is LOCAL only when the old path does not reproduce itself end to end (its A/A
    # fails the end-to-end test: the reference cannot judge the fast path), else 'full'. (_fast_guard_mode, fast_lora_guard)
    fast_guard=env("FAST_GUARD", "full"),
    fast_merge=env("FAST_MERGE", False, bool),         # ours (T016/speed): with FAST_LORA, W' = W + s U D built without a copy
                                                       # of W and with one rounding into a compute-dtype buffer (_fm_merge),
                                                       # bit-identical to Comfy's merge; per module verified against it once
                                                       # after the first optimizer step (_fm_verify); 0 = Comfy's merge
    # ours (T091, 13 Oct; speed): FAST_WCACHE - with FAST_LORA, the base weight the fast path rebuilds in the compute dtype
    # on every forward (FAST_MERGE's W', FAST_FWD's x W^T) and every backward (grad_x) - ideogram4: the dequantize of an
    # fp8 QuantizedTensor (comfy_kitchen eager: a cast, then x scale: two full passes; UNC_TRAIN leaves every LoRA weight at a
    # recalculated scale), qwen-image: the cast of a plain fp8 weight - is kept after its first rebuild, inside a memory
    # budget fixed after the first optimizer step: total - resident - the activation room - FAST_WCACHE_MARGIN GiB, the room
    # FAST_WCACHE_PROBE x the task's largest case measured before member 1 (T095 memory probe, fast_mem_probe: step 1 is no
    #
    # on 13 Oct), FAST_WCACHE_ACT x step 1's activations without a probe (T091); FAST_WCACHE_GIB > 0: that budget instead.
    # Only the training compute dtype is kept. An out-of-memory step with kept rebuilds first drops them all (no refill) and
    # redoes the step with the same draws (case, noise, sampler records: _wcache_snap) - unless the optimizer update had
    # started (T095: then no redo, no second update) - before the OOM path's checkpointing; before an evaluator-exact merge
    # (holdout evals, score_sd_exact, scale search, TE drop check), the TE merge, RRF and at the end of training the kept
    # rebuilds are given back (_wcache_release; refilled by later training steps). The kept tensor is the rebuild's own
    # output and the base weights are frozen (a swapped weight object is never served from the cache), so every byte
    # downstream is unchanged. 0 = the trainer unchanged.
    fast_wcache=env("FAST_WCACHE", False, bool),
    fast_wcache_margin=env("FAST_WCACHE_MARGIN", 6.0, float),
    fast_wcache_act=env("FAST_WCACHE_ACT", 1.7, float),
    fast_wcache_gib=env("FAST_WCACHE_GIB", 0.0, float),
