    # set_checkpointing wraps), installed once before the first member (compile_blocks_setup); needs FAST_LORA (its guard
    # passed). Every FAST_LORA Linear in a block (its first-use check passed) is the opaque custom op g56cb::lora_linear whose
    # kernels are the trainer's own _fast_forward / _fast_backward (FAST_MERGE / FAST_WCACHE / FAST_FWD / FAST_MCACHE
    # unchanged, no graph break); any other Linear runs eagerly behind torch.compiler.disable (a graph break). Compiled are
    # the ops between them (norms, modulation, rope, attention, activations, residuals: fused kernels, other bf16
    # rounding). Only training forwards with grad on take the compiled path; every no-grad forward (holdout scoring,
    # RB_EMPTY's caption forward, RRF) is eager. Setup on probe cases of the task (caption lengths / latent shapes) with
    # probe LoRA factors (|s U D| = 0.1 |W| as the FAST_LORA guard's, restored after): eager vs compiled forward + backward -
    # output, pooled LoRA gradients and every module group's within _CB_TOL - then the timed A/B; kept only when compiled
