    # (fg_inject at write time: never averaged or scaled). A guidance-distilled output at g is not E[v | x_t, c] (the MSE
    #
    guidance_remap=env("GUIDANCE_REMAP", 0.0, float),
    # ours (T050, 7 Oct): last.safetensors (all but the interim saves while a member trains) stores each LoRA module in its
    # canonical SVD factorization (canon_sd): the same product up @ down at the same rank and alpha, i.e. the same delta for
    # ComfyUI's loader, with balanced factors ordered by singular value. 0 = the trainer unchanged.
    canon=env("CANON", False, bool),
    # ours (T058, 7 Oct): GENCOND 1 - generator-conditional defaults. main() tells which image generator made the task's
    # training images from their shapes alone (gen_detect) and applies FAMILY_DEFAULTS_GEN[family][generator] after the
    # family and task-size defaults (gencond_setup; explicit G56CT_* env vars still win). 0 = off: no detection, the map is
    # ignored, the trainer unchanged.
    gencond=env("GENCOND", 0, int),
    # ours (stage 9, 18 Oct): BASECOND 1 - base-conditional defaults. main() reads the root checkpoint's probe dtype from its
    # header (base_root_dtype) and applies FAMILY_DEFAULTS_BASE[family][dtype] right after the generator cell (basecond_setup;
    # explicit G56CT_* env vars still win). 0 = off: nothing read, the map ignored, the trainer unchanged.
    basecond=env("BASECOND", 0, int),
    # ours (T063, 11 Oct): RRF 1 - readout refit of the shipped average in the time left after the last member
    # (rrf_finalize, comfytrain/rrf.py): closed-form ridge corrections of the final readout (output bias; the sigma-dependent
    # shift through the final modulation's shift rows for flux / qwen-image; the final Linear where ComfyUI merges it by a
    # plain cast) fitted on the training images, lambda / form by 5-fold CV over the images, written only when the CV gain
    # survives the evaluator's merge. RRF_BANDS: sigma bands per (image, prompt) - 8 = the alternating half of the 16
    # midpoints (every band on half of the images; half the forwards). RRF_TIME_FRAC: runs only when that many times its
    # estimated duration (+ the write) fit before the deadline (r12x8a production-form logs: 8 bands x 1.5 -> acts in 22 of
    # 35 runs, 16 bands x 2.0 -> 9 of 35). 0 = off: nothing runs, the trainer unchanged.
    rrf=env("RRF", False, bool),
    rrf_bands=env("RRF_BANDS", 8, int),
    rrf_time_frac=env("RRF_TIME_FRAC", 1.5, float),
    #
    #
    # training images, as one seeded, shuffled (image, band, half) schedule whose length is the members' step cap (all-data
    # mode; an explicit G56CT_MAX_STEPS wins) - instead of the uniform (image, band) walk with alternating prompts. 'flux' /
    # 'ideogram4' / 'z-image' = that family's table (EXPOSURE_TABLES), or a spec like 't0-3:4.01,t4-13:2.01,...,e14-15:6.01'
    # covering each (half, band) once. Needs PROMPT_MODE=balanced (one case per step); else one private 'exposure: off (...)'
    # line (exposure_setup, Exposure). LR pilots (G56CT_LR_PILOT) keep the uniform walk, LR_PILOT_FRAC x this cap long (the
    # cap is set before them): they choose the LR on another walk than the members'. 'off' = the trainer unchanged.
    exposure=env("EXPOSURE", "off"),
